    "content": "Valerie Perrine, the actress known for playing Eve Teschmacher in the 1978 Superman film and its sequel, died on March 23, 2026, at age 82. She passed away at her home after a long battle with Parkinson's disease. Perrine was an Oscar-nominated actress known for her roles in Lenny and The Electric Horseman. Key Details Regarding Valerie Perrine's Passing: Role: She played Eve Teschmacher, Lex Luthor's (Gene Hackman) accomplice in Superman (1978) and Superman II (1980) Newsweek. Cause of Death: She had been battling Parkinson’s disease for over 15 years, as reported on AOL.com and by USA Today. Career Highlights: In addition to Superman, she won Best Actress at the Cannes Film Festival and earned an Oscar nomination for her role in 1974's Lenny Newsweek. Legacy: A 2019 documentary, Valerie, explored her career and health struggles according to USA Today. Note: This refers to the passing of Valerie Perrine in March 2026. Other Superman actresses, such as Margot Kidder (Lois Lane), passed away in 2018, as reported on YouTube and by 11Alive.com.",
